WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:06.180
"Loki'' has been a massive success for Marvel
Studios and Disney+, and the series remains

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.390
popular with the die-hard MCU fans.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:14.830
The penultimate episode, "Journey Into Mystery"
— itself a nod to the name of the 1960s

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:20.050
comic book in which Loki and Thor first appeared
– was full of "Loki'' Easter eggs that had

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:25.480
fans across the internet dissecting every
frame to find fun little comic book nods.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:30.119
This was particularly true of the vast wasteland
in the void at the end of time, which was

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:34.900
full of MCU relics, including the Dark Aster
— which is a ship that is associated with

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.270
Ronan The Accuser, Yellowjacket's helmet — remember
him?

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.710
From Ant-Man, and the remains of a ruined
Avengers Tower.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:44.859
This is called Qeng — an intriguing easter
egg itself.

00:00:44.859 --> 00:00:49.789
In the comics, Qeng Enterprises bought the
old Avengers Building from Tony Stark, and

00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:54.220
it turns out that Qeng had a direct relationship
with Kang the Conqueror!

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.269
The Kang-MCU rumors have been floating around
for years now.

00:00:57.269 --> 00:01:01.539
We also met a whole new gaggle of Loki variants,
in addition to the group which debuted in

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:03.640
the Episode 4 post-credits scene.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.990
While spotting the Thanos Copter in the void
was one of the coolest Easter eggs in the

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:12.210
entire MCU, because who doesn’t love them
some Thanos Copter?

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:16.410
— There was one other that joined it at
the top of the ranks.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:20.840
Episode 5 pulled one of the most beloved — and
often poked fun at — characters straight

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:24.100
from the Marvel pages and threw him right
into "Loki."

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.860
This moment was also doubly special as it
included a special cameo from Chris Hemsworth

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.430
himself, which many viewers of the episode
likely missed.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:36.630
Just shy of 10 minutes into Episode 5, Loki
is traveling with his newfound group of fellow

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.140
Lokis, bound for the shelter of their underground
bunker.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.790
As the camera pans from above ground to the
hidden lair, a major Easter egg hides in the

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:45.790
dirt.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:51.770
Stuck in a jar that reads T365 is a miniature
Thor, who turns out to be the Toad of Thunder:

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:54.590
Throg . Guess you could say that the jar is
some sort of…

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:55.590
“Frog protection.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:56.590
Fraud protection.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.590
Yeah, frog, fraud, frog, fraud.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.810
I think we’re on the same page.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.270
We’re totally on the same page”

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:05.750
The tiny — but mighty — amphibian jumps
around in the jar, attempting to reach Mjolnir.

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:09.099
While he does this, he lets out a few grunts
of frustration.

00:02:09.099 --> 00:02:13.400
And according to "Loki" director Kate Herron,
these grunts were actually recorded by Chris

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.790
Hemsworth himself!

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:19.790
Herron clarified that these noises were not
recycled from any previous films - Hemsworth

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:24.370
actually did all new voice work - well, grunt-work,
just for Loki.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:28.390
Fans were hoping to get some sort of cameo
from the Australian actor in "Loki," and this

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:33.200
was just the perfect way to do it without
having him steal the spotlight from his on-screen

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.200
brother.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.749
“Sorry about that time I turned you into
a frog.”

00:02:36.749 --> 00:02:38.430
“It was a wonderful joke!”

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.880
As "Loki" writer Eric Martin revealed during
his live-tweet screening of Episode 5, fans

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.819
could have seen Throg much sooner.

00:02:44.819 --> 00:02:50.620
"We actually shot a scene for the Time Theater
in Ep 1 of Loki getting pummeled by Frog Thor,

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.909
but had to cut it to keep things moving.

00:02:52.909 --> 00:02:55.349
It's too bad, because Tom was funny as hell."

00:02:55.349 --> 00:02:59.959
Hemsworth will also lend his voice to Thor
in the upcoming MCU series, "What If...?,"

00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:03.739
which is set to debut on Disney+ on August
11th.

